WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.067
-Welcome back, everybody.
Here at "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:06.567
We love stand-up comedy
and we especially love stand-up

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:09.367
written by our audience members
in under an hour.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:12.501
That's right. It's time for a
battle of the instant stand-ups.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.601
Here we go.

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:16.968
-♪ Battle of the instant
stand-ups ♪

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:19.534
-Welcome to "Battle
of the Instant Stand-ups."

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.267
Before the show,
we went through our audience

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.234
and picked out two people
who said they were comedians.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.734
We gave them each a topic
and then gave them an hour

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:30.167
to write an original stand-up
set based on that topic.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.501
They've never performed it.

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.701
Here they are preparing
backstage a minute ago.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:36.701
Yeah. You can't unsee that.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.734
Now, let's see what they came up
with and meet them right now.

00:00:39.734 --> 00:00:42.000
Come on over, everybody.
Guys, come on out.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:44.901
Nice to see you.

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.567
Nice to see you. Pleasure.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:51.434
Hi. Nice to see you.
Welcome to the show.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:54.100
Now, let's start
with contestant number one.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.367
What is your name
and where are you from?

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.901
-I'm Nat Towson, and I'm
from Manhattan, New York.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hey! From Manhattan, New York.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:03.400
I love that.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.734
-Nat, what was the topic
that you were given tonight?

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.467
-Saint Patrick's Day.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.901
-Okay, and are you Irish?
Or we'll find out, I guess.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.868
-I'm not.
-Yeah. Interesting.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.367
And you've never performed
this in front of a crowd?

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.567
You just wrote this?
-Yeah.

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:15.734
-This is very exciting.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:16.801
Alright, well, head
on over to the stage.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.367
Get in your headspace.
Nat.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:22.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:26.300
This is exciting. I love this.
And now, ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.133
here to perform
a brand-new comedy

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.133
set about Saint Patrick's Day,

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:32.434
Please give it up
for Nat Towson.

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:35.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.200
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.601
I just got back from Europe.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.534
I know I look like
I was about to say that.

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.167
I learned that in Ireland,

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:49.868
Saint Patrick's Day is actually
not a big deal at all.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:51.767
They already have a day
when everyone drinks.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.067
It's called Monday.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:54.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:59.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.801
Last year, I spent
Saint Patrick's Day

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:04.100
with 3,000 drunk idiots
in Midtown Manhattan.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.100
-Whoo!

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.467
-No place has been
that disrespectful

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.067
to the Irish since England.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:16.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:18.434
It's true. The English
hate redheads so much,

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:20.334
they don't even like
Prince Harry.

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:24.968
And everyone in Midtown
was dressed

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:29.000
in traditional
Celtic Mardi Gras beads...

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:34.734
...and a T-shirt that said,
"I-rish you were naked."

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:38.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.334
I-rish I was making that up.

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:43.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.801
And everyone was wearing green,

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.868
so you couldn't even tell
which frat they were in.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.200
And then they all
scurried off to New Jersey...

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:56.267
...like the snakes fleeing
Ireland.

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:59.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:00.734
Meanwhile, in Dublin,

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.601
everyone just had
a couple of pints at the pub

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:05.033
and then headed to a museum
to see the body of a man

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:07.534
who died in a bog
in 400 B.C.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:13.133
And in America we celebrate
by peeing in an ATM.

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.501
Thank you so much.
I'm Nat Towson.

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:18.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
-There we go. Thank you, bud.

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.968
Nat Towson, everybody.
Thank you very much.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.901
That was amazing.
I appreciate it.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.601
Let's meet
contestant number two.

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.467
What is your name
and where are you from?

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:30.534
-I'm Allison Reese,
and I am from Mesa, Arizona.

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:35.400
-Hey, Arizona.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.067
Alright. Can you tell
everyone what your topic is?

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.701
-Yes. Spring break.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:41.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.167
-Alright, bud. This is good.

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.033
Arizona's got some good spring
breaking out there.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:46.234
They got some good party
schools.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:48.234
-Yeah. ASU.
-ASU, exactly.

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:49.701
-They're so into it.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:49.701 --> 00:03:51.267
Alright, get over. Get ready.

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:52.801
Get in your headspace.
Be prepared.

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:54.601
Thank you for doing this and
let me know when you're ready.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:55.901
Okay. Channel the zone.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.100
Channel the inspiration.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:03.367
Ladies and gentlemen, here
to perform a brand-new comedy

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:07.834
set about spring break is
the one and only Allison Reese!

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:11.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.067
-Yes. Thank you. Thank you.

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:17.801
Yes. I've never been
a spring break person.

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:21.834
You know? I'm really more
of a "Kohl's Cash counts

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:26.267
as real money" kind of a person,
you know.

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:30.067
But Florida spring break
seems cool, right?

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:33.300
They got beaches,
drinking, gators.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.467
That pet possum with lipstick
on it.

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:40.434
Florida's got all your spring
break needs, you know.

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:43.200
If I ever went
to a spring break concert,

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.234
though, I think I'd want
to see Maroon 5.

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:49.901
[ Crowd cheers ]
Yeah, right? Yeah.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:52.667
But I want to see Maroon 5
solely

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:56.334
because I think that the guy
in Maroon 5 sounds like if

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:59.767
for the last five years, Elmo
has been taking testosterone.

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:02.434
[ Laughter ]
You know?

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:03.801
Like, can't you hear it?

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:07.901
[ High-pitched voice]
♪ And she will be loved ♪

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:12.334
♪ Tap on my window,
knock on my door ♪

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.934
[ As Elmo ] Elmo want to make
you feel beautiful.

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:17.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:20.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:22.033
That tickles.

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:25.467
[ Normal voice ] Oh, man, you
can't tell me that guy

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:26.701
doesn't sound like Elmo.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:27.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:29.601
Later you're going to be
listening to Maroon 5,

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:32.100
and you're going
to be like, "Elmo?

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.868
Elmo, your voice dropped."

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:36.901
Honestly, it's the only
spring break concert

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:39.434
I'm spending
my Kohl's Cash on, so yeah.

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:41.667
Thank you so much.
I'm Allison Reese.

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:44.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Come on, Allison!

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.133
Allison Reese once again.

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:48.434
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:51.701
Now it is time
to see who won.

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:54.667
So we're going to let our great
audience decide the winner.

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:55.801
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:55.801 --> 00:05:58.801
Was it Nat Towson?

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:02.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:04.467
Or was it Allison Reese?

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:08.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.701
The winner is Alison Reese!
Congratulations.

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:16.133
You'll be going home --
You'll be going home

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:18.167
with an
"I love jokes" sweatshirt.

00:06:18.167 --> 00:06:19.501
Congratulations.
-Oh, man.

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:22.167
-Yes. Congratulations.

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:25.334
You also take
a Tonight Show notebook

00:06:25.334 --> 00:06:29.334
for writing more comedy
and $1,000 cash.

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:33.767
Come on, bud. Allison Reese,
thank you so much.

00:06:33.767 --> 00:06:35.367
But no one goes home
empty-handed.

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:37.033
Our other contestant will also

00:06:37.033 --> 00:06:39.200
get an "I love jokes"
sweatshirt.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.667
There you go.
Nat, you deserve it.

00:06:42.667 --> 00:06:45.133
And a Tonight Show notebook
and $1,000.

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:49.234
Give it up for two new instant
stand-up comedians.

00:06:49.234 --> 00:06:52.367
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Tessa Thompson.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:53.634
Come on back, everybody.

